# DRM Notes

## What I was trying to do
Understand how Linux handles displays, modesetting, and GPU access.

## What I started with
- drm-kms docs
- Intel DRM search results

## What each part does
- KMS: sets display modes
- GEM/TTM: memory management
- IOCTLs: communication with the kernel

## What happened
- DRM is low-level but powerful.
- KMS makes sense once you see the flow.

## What confused me
- Plane/CRTC/encoder relationships.
- Buffer lifetime rules.

## What I want to try next
- Write a tiny KMS program.
- Explore Intel’s DRM driver.

## Random thoughts
DRM is the “bare metal” of Linux graphics.
